<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="lede">Last updated: 19 August 2026.</p>

<div class="prose">
  <h2>Who handles your data</h2>
  <p>The data controller is María Pía Peña Foissac, who runs this site under the name tuaccesible. For anything to do with your data, the channel is <a href="mailto:contacto@tuaccesible.com">contacto@tuaccesible.com</a>.</p>
  <p>tuaccesible works from Argentina, a country the European Commission recognises with an adequacy decision. In practice that means a client in the European Union can send us personal data without signing standard contractual clauses or putting any other transfer mechanism in place.</p>

  <h2>What we collect and what for</h2>
  <p>Only what you type in yourself. This site has no user accounts, no cart, no private area, and no forms beyond the two below.</p>
  <h3>Contact form</h3>
  <p>We collect your name, your email, the service you are interested in and your message. We use them to reply to you and, if we agree to work together, to put a quote together.</p>
  <h3>Review form</h3>
  <p>We collect the name or initials you want published, the service you hired, two ratings, an optional comment and your explicit permission. We use them to publish the review, always after checking it: nothing goes live automatically.</p>

  <h2>The legal basis</h2>
  <p>Contact enquiries are handled to take steps at your request before entering into a contract, which is what asking for a quote is. If your message does not lead to any work, the basis is our legitimate interest in replying to people who write to us.</p>
  <p>Reviews are handled with your consent, which you give explicitly in the form and can withdraw at any time without giving a reason.</p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>Both forms are processed by Web3Forms, a provider acting as our data processor, whose servers are in the United States. That means an international transfer of data outside the European Economic Area. Web3Forms delivers the message to our inbox; it does not publish it on any open dashboard.</p>
  <p>The inbox where we receive messages is hosted by Arsys (Arsys Internet S.L.U., Spain), which also acts as a processor.</p>
  <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs the IP address of anyone visiting any site hosted there, for security reasons. That log belongs to GitHub, not to us: we have no access to it and make no use of it.</p>
  <p>Beyond those three, nobody. There is no advertising, no embedded social media, and no other third-party piece loading on these pages.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Enquiries are kept for as long as the conversation lasts and up to twelve months afterwards, in case you pick the thread back up. Published reviews are kept for as long as they stay published; if you withdraw your permission, they come down.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>We use no analytics of any kind: no Google Analytics, no other visit-counting tool. We use no cookies, first-party or third-party. We do not sell or pass on your data for advertising. We do not profile anyone or make automated decisions about anyone.</p>

  <h2>The one thing stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>If you pick a language, the site saves that preference in your own browser local storage, under the key <code>tuaccesible-lang-choice</code>. It is not a cookie, it never travels to any server, it identifies nobody, and its only effect is that we will not suggest a language change you already turned down. You can clear it from your browser settings and the site carries on working the same.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask for access to your data, for it to be corrected or deleted; you can restrict or object to us handling it, ask us to hand it over in a format you can take elsewhere, and withdraw any consent you have given. It all works by writing to <a href="mailto:contacto@tuaccesible.com">contacto@tuaccesible.com</a>, and we reply within one month at the latest.</p>
  <p>If you think we are handling your data badly, you can complain to the supervisory authority in your country. In Spain that is the <span lang="es">Agencia Española de Protección de Datos</span>.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If anything changes, the date above changes too. If the change affects what we do with your data rather than just the wording, we say so on this page.</p>
</div>
